I get criticized by MAGA Republicans for criticizing Trump. But if Republicans don't criticize Trump, then the only criticism will come from Democrats. But Democrats criticize Trump for the wrong reasons. Letting Democrats define Trump undermines the Republican cause. 

I criticize Trump for being too much like Democrats. Republicans need to draw a contrast between the failed big-government policies of Trump and Democrats and the true free-market, limited-government policies that should define the party.

@ChuckNash66 Government is spending and borrowing more under Trump than it was under Biden. So Trump has helped make government bigger, not smaller.

The Sept. U.S. trade deficit in goods was $134.9 billion, the highest ever recorded in Sept. There were only three months in history when the deficit was higher, all under Trump in 2025.   

Here are the facts. Measured by the size of our trade deficits, Trump has been the worst president in history on trade. The tariffs have been a complete failure. Not only have they failed to bring manufacturing back to the U.S., but the U.S. is now more dependent than ever on foreign producers. Not only are we importing more than ever, but we are now paying Trump's tariffs on those imports. 

Trump says trade deficits represent a loss. Judged by his own standard, Trump is the biggest loser in the history of the presidency. Also, if the economy is booming as Republicans claim, why have our trade deficits gone way up? Why are the trade deficits under Trump so much larger than they were under Biden, when, according to Trump, we had the worst economy in U.S. history?  

Here are the facts. When you compare Trump's first two years to Biden's last two, GDP growth and job creation are slower, inflation is higher, and budget and trade deficits are bigger. If Trump is right that under Biden we had the worst economy in history, and the Trump economy is objectively worse on all counts, then the Trump economy is now the worst economy in history.

@MatthewSWagner I am no fan of Biden. He was a bad president. But judged by his own standards, so is Trump.

@AmerShouaeb I'm just holding Trump to his own standards.

@MitchBloxx The stated goal of the tariffs was to reduce our trade deficits. Since are trade deficits are now larger than ever, they tariffs failed. If we really had a booming economy, we would be producing more and importing less. Instead, we are going into debt to live beyond our means.

@MitchBloxx Yes, but by other metrics the Trump economy is also weaker than the Biden economy. That is the point of my post.

@smithwbrian68 It's not one month, it's every month. Cumulatively the trade deficits are larger under Trump than the were under Biden.

